      "text": "Crosslake grew after the 1885 construction of the Pine River Dam, which spurred development.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Crosslake%2C_Minnesota"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town’s early settlers were drawn by Northern Minnesota’s booming logging industry.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Crosslake%2C_Minnesota"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Originally part of Cass County’s Watertown Township, Crosslake became part of Crow Wing County in 1887.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1,
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Crosslake%2C_Minnesota"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The township split into Crosslake Village in 1951, North Crosslake Village in 1964, and finally merged into the City of Crosslake in 1974.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10,
        11,
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Crosslake%2C_Minnesota"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Crosslake sits within the Brainerd Lakes Area, surrounded by nearly 460 lakes within a 25‑mile radius of Brainerd.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Crosslake%2C_Minnesota"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Main routes through Crosslake include County Roads 3, 16, 36, 66, and 103, linking it to neighboring communities.",
